{"step_index":102,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:46:28Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Updated walkthrough documenting the interface improvements for StreamWave Entertainment.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Walkthrough: StreamWave Entertainment Interface Refinements\n\nThe **StreamWave Entertainment** user interface has been enhanced with professional, accessible, and responsive design features without modifying the working FastAPI backend or Vercel serverless architecture.\n\n---\n\n## 🎨 Interface Improvements Summary\n\n### 1. Playback Labels & Technical Clarity\n- **Contextual Action Labels**: Movies now display **\"🎬 Watch Preview\"** while music titles display **\"🎵 Play Sample\"**. The hero feature section dynamically uses **\"🎬 Watch Preview\"** for *Cook Off*.\n- **Technical Sample Badges**: Added discreet **\"Technical Sample\"** tags to cards and modals to clarify academic usage of synthesized audio without implying copyrighted streaming content.\n\n### 2. Header & Developer Navigation\n- **Discreet Badge**: Scaled down the **\"Serverless Demo\"** badge into a clean pill indicator (`.serverless-badge-sm`).\n- **Developer Link**: Replaced the prominent API Docs link with a compact **`Developer ↗`** nav button opening `/docs`.\n\n### 3. Media Cards & Grid Layout\n- **2-Line Clamped Titles**: Long titles wrap up to 2 lines (`-webkit-line-clamp: 2`) without early truncation, complete with native `title=\"...\"` hover tooltips.\n- **Interactive Thumbnails & Titles**: Clicking the cover image or card title directly opens the media details modal.\n- **Subtle Micro-Interactions**: Hover scale effects (`transform: scale(1.04)`) and crisp `:focus-visible` outline indicators.\n\n### 4. Audio Player & Footer\n- **Bottom Space Clearance**: Added `padding-bottom: 110px` to `body` ensuring the fixed audio bar never obscures content or footer text.\n- **Mobile Collapse Toggle**: Integrated a mobile minimize/expand button (`#player-toggle-btn`).\n- **Academic Disclaimer Footer**: Added an explicit footer explaining the non-commercial academic nature of the prototype.\n\n### 5. Responsive Grid Breakdown\n- **Large Desktops (≥1200px)**: 4 columns.\n- **Medium Desktops (900px – 1199px)**: 3 columns.\n- **Tablets (600px – 899px)**: 2 columns.\n- **Mobile Screens (<600px)**: 1 column.\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Files Modified\n\n| File | Changes Made |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| [`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/index.html) | Added `Developer ↗` link, discreet serverless badge, hero tags, accessible `<aside>` audio bar, minimize button, and academic disclaimer footer. |\n| [`public/css/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/css/styles.css) | Implemented 4-3-2-1 responsive CSS grid, 2-line title clamping, clickable covers, `:focus-visible` rings, reduced motion queries, and player bar minimization. |\n| [`public/js/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/js/app.js) | Added dynamic \"Watch Preview\" / \"Play Sample\" label logic, tooltip attributes, cover click handlers, dialog `Escape` key support, and player minimize toggle. |\n","Description":"Update walkthrough.md with interface refinements documentation","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Updating walkthrough.md","toolSummary":"Updating walkthrough.md"}}]}
