{"step_index":104,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:46:42Z","content":"I have completed the user interface refinements for **StreamWave Entertainment** while fully preserving all working FastAPI endpoints, data structures, Pydantic schemas, unit tests, and Vercel serverless configurations.\n\n---\n\n### 📂 Files Modified\n\n1. [`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/index.html): Updated header layout, discreet `Serverless Demo` badge, compact `Developer ↗` link, hero tags, accessible audio player structure, mobile minimize toggle, and non-commercial academic disclaimer footer.\n2. [`public/css/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/css/styles.css): Added 4-3-2-1 column responsive CSS grid, 2-line title clamping (`-webkit-line-clamp: 2`), `:focus-visible` accessibility rings, reduced motion query support, page bottom clearance (`110px`), and dark graphite visual hierarchy.\n3. [`public/js/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/js/app.js): Implemented type-aware playback labels (**Watch Preview** vs **Play Sample**), card title tooltips, clickable thumbnails/titles, Escape key modal support, and mobile player minimization.\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Summary of Interface Improvements\n\n1. **Contextual Playback Labels & Technical Clarity**:\n   - Movie items now display **\"🎬 Watch Preview\"**.\n   - Music items now display **\"🎵 Play Sample\"**.\n   - Featured hero section (*Cook Off*) displays **\"🎬 Watch Preview\"**.\n   - Cards and details modals feature a discreet **\"Technical Sample\"** badge to clarify academic audio usage.\n\n2. **Header & Navigation**:\n   - Scaled down the serverless badge into a subtle green-pulsing pill (`Serverless Demo`).\n   - Replaced the primary API Docs link with a compact **`Developer ↗`** button pointing to `/docs`.\n\n3. **Media Cards & Responsive Grid Layout**:\n   - **4 Columns** on Large Desktops (`≥1200px`)\n   - **3 Columns** on Medium Desktops (`900px – 1199px`)\n   - **2 Columns** on Tablets (`600px – 899px`)\n   - **1 Column** on Mobile Screens (`<600px`)\n   - Card titles occupy up to 2 lines with native `title=\"...\"` tooltips.\n   - Cover thumbnails and titles are clickable to open details.\n\n4. **Audio Player & Page Clearance**:\n   - Added `padding-bottom: 110px` on `body` ensuring the fixed audio bar never obscures content or footer text.\n   - Added a minimize/expand toggle button (`▼` / `▲`) for mobile viewports.\n\n5. **Accessibility & Academic Disclosure**:\n   - High-contrast text on dark graphite (`#121214`), visible `:focus-visible` focus rings, Escape key modal closing, and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` support.\n   - Added an explicit footer statement clarifying the platform as a non-commercial academic serverless prototype.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Test & Manual Verification Results\n\n- **Automated Tests**: 100% passing (All 12 unit tests in `tests/test_api.py` passed with 0 errors and 0 warnings).\n- **Manual Verification**:\n  - **Search & Filtering**: Searching queries (e.g. `Cook`, `stream`) and filtering by media type (**Movies** / **Music**) or genre (**Zimdancehall**, **Comedy**) functions dynamically.\n  - **Details Modal**: Opens with complete title/description and closes on `Escape` key press or close button click.\n  - **Playback & Events**: Clicking **Watch Preview** or **Play Sample** loads `/media/demo.wav` into the audio bar and triggers `POST /api/play-events`.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Remaining Limitations\n\n1. **Academic Demonstration Audio**: All media cards utilize the synthesized 3-second non-copyrighted WAV chime for academic compliance.\n2. **Ephemeral Playback Logs**: Playback events are logged via Python `logger.info()` to Vercel Runtime Logs and stdout without database persistence."}
{"step_index":105,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:02:29Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nUpdate the existing StreamWave FastAPI project so that the completed five-second StreamWave MP4 video is used as the preview for every movie when a user clicks “Watch Preview”.\r\n\r\nDo not rebuild the application or replace its working FastAPI backend. First inspect the existing project structure, catalogue data, playback buttons, modal system and `/api/play-events` endpoint.\r\n\r\nIMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS\r\n\r\n1. VIDEO ASSET\r\n\r\n* Locate the completed five-second StreamWave MP4 file I have added to the project.\r\n* If it is not already in the correct static directory, place it in:\r\n  `public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\r\n* Do not modify, regenerate or compress the original video unless browser playback fails because of an unsupported format.\r\n* Use the relative public URL:\r\n  `/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\r\n* The browser must retrieve the video directly as a static asset. Do not proxy video bytes through FastAPI.\r\n\r\n2. MOVIE CATALOGUE\r\n\r\n* Configure every item whose media type is `movie` to use the same StreamWave preview video.\r\n* Add a `preview_url` field to movie records if the current data model does not already contain one.\r\n* Ensure all movie records use:\r\n  `/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`\r\n* Do not replace the existing music demonstration audio.\r\n* Music items must continue using the audio player and the “Play Sample” button.\r\n* Movie items must use the “Watch Preview” button.\r\n\r\n3. VIDEO PLAYER\r\n\r\n* When a user clicks “Watch Preview” on any movie card or featured movie, open a professional video-player modal.\r\n* Display the selected movie’s title above the video.\r\n* Load the shared StreamWave preview into an HTML5 `<video>` element.\r\n* Start playback automatically because it follows a direct user click.\r\n* Include `controls`, `playsinline` and `preload=\"metadata\"`.\r\n* Preserve the video’s original 16:9 aspect ratio.\r\n* Use a black player background and prevent stretching or distortion.\r\n* Do not loop the video automatically.\r\n* When the five-second preview ends, show a clear Replay button and Close button.\r\n\r\n4. MODAL BEHAVIOUR\r\n\r\n* Allow the user to close the video using:\r\n\r\n  * The Close button.\r\n  * A top-right close icon.\r\n  * The Escape key.\r\n  * Clicking the backdrop, provided the click is outside the player.\r\n* When the modal closes, pause the video, reset it to 0 seconds and clear the active movie.\r\n* Prevent page scrolling while the modal is open.\r\n* Return keyboard focus to the button that opened the modal.\r\n* Trap keyboard focus inside the modal while it is open.\r\n* Add appropriate ARIA labels and dialog attributes.\r\n\r\n5. PLAYBACK LOGGING\r\n\r\n* When movie playback begins, call the existing `/api/play-events` endpoint using the selected movie’s actual media ID.\r\n* Do not create fake database records.\r\n* Preserve the existing structured runtime logging.\r\n* Ensure one user click does not generate duplicate playback events.\r\n* Do not break music playback-event logging.\r\n\r\n6. USER INTERFACE\r\n\r\n* Keep the existing dark graphite, white and red StreamWave visual style.\r\n* Make the video modal responsive on desktop, tablet and mobile.\r\n* Maximum player width should be approximately 960 pixels while remaining within the viewport.\r\n* On mobile, use nearly the full screen width with accessible controls.\r\n* Display a small label stating “5-second technical preview” so users understand that it is an academic demonstration.\r\n* Do not add excessive animation, glowing effects or unnecessary visual elements.\r\n\r\n7. TECHNICAL VERIFICATION\r\n   Test and confirm:\r\n\r\n* Every movie card opens the same five-second video.\r\n* The featured movie opens the same video.\r\n* Music cards still open the audio player.\r\n* The correct movie title appears in the modal.\r\n* The video returns HTTP 200.\r\n* The browser receives an appropriate `video/mp4` content type.\r\n* Playback starts after the user click.\r\n* Replay works after the video ends.\r\n* Closing the modal stops and resets playback.\r\n* Escape-key closing works.\r\n* Playback logging generates only one event per playback start.\r\n* The interface remains responsive.\r\n* Existing API and automated tests continue to pass.\r\n\r\nAdd or update automated tests where practical, update the README with the video-preview behaviour and report:\r\n\r\n1. Files changed.\r\n2. The final video path.\r\n3. Tests performed and their actual results.\r\n4. Whether local video playback was verified.\r\n5. Any remaining limitation.\r\n\r\nDo not claim successful playback unless it has actually been tested in the browser. the video is in the downloads \r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T20:02:29+02:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
