{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:03:29Z","thinking":"**Examining the File**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the video file located at `C:\\Users\\dell\\Downloads\\Use_the_uploaded_StreamWave_lo.mp4`. I'm starting the investigation of this specific file.\n\n\n**Copying the Video**\n\nI'm now focused on copying the video file. I've located the file and path and am now examining methods for transferring it. Initially, I considered several options: writing a Python script, using a command, or even byte-level manipulation. Ultimately, I'm leaning toward creating a script for the copy operation and I will write a Python script `scratch/copy_video.py` or use python to read the file and write bytes.\n\n\n**Implementing the Copy**\n\nI've decided to create `scripts/copy_preview_video.py` using `shutil.copyfile` to transfer the video. The script also includes a check to ensure the source file exists. I'll test this and plan to integrate a copy operation in `app.py`'s initialization if the target doesn't exist. Now I'm ensuring all the user requirements are met.\n\n\n**Designing the Video Player**\n\nI'm now deeply involved in the video player design, including the modal and its behavior. I'm focusing on implementing a dedicated modal using a `<dialog>` element. I will display movie titles, labels stating that it is a \"5-second technical preview\", and the required HTML5 `<video>` element with specific styling (aspect ratio, background, object-fit). I'm also planning the controls for closing the modal: close buttons, escape key, and backdrop clicks, with the necessary pause and reset actions. I am planning the `<video>` element's autoplay, and event listeners.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCopies the StreamWave 5-second MP4 demonstration video from Downloads\nto the static public media directory (public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport shutil\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nTARGET_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"public\" / \"media\"\nTARGET_FILE = TARGET_DIR / \"streamwave-preview.mp4\"\n\n# Candidate source paths in user Downloads folder\nDOWNLOADS_DIR = Path(r\"C:\\Users\\dell\\Downloads\")\nCANDIDATE_SOURCES = [\n    DOWNLOADS_DIR / \"Use_the_uploaded_StreamWave_lo.mp4\",\n    DOWNLOADS_DIR / \"Download (28).mp4\",\n]\n\n\ndef copy_preview_video() -> bool:\n    TARGET_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    for source in CANDIDATE_SOURCES:\n        if source.exists() and source.stat().st_size > 0:\n            shutil.copyfile(source, TARGET_FILE)\n            print(\n                f\"✅ Successfully copied video asset:\\n  Source: {source}\\n  Target: {TARGET_FILE} ({TARGET_FILE.stat().st_size} bytes)\"\n            )\n            return True\n\n    print(\"⚠️ No candidate video source found in Downloads directory.\")\n    return False\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    copy_preview_video()\n","Description":"Create script to locate and copy StreamWave preview MP4 video to public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\scripts\\copy_preview_video.py","toolAction":"Creating script to copy preview video","toolSummary":"Creating script to copy preview video"}}]}
